      "year": 2025,
      "problem_number": 3,
      "statement_en": "Fix an integer n ≥ 3. Determine the smallest positive integer k\nsatisfying the following condition:\nFor any tree T with vertices v1, v2, . . . , vn and any pairwise dis-\ntinct complex numbersz1, z2, . . . , zn, there is a polynomialP (X, Y )\nwith complex coefficients of total degree at most k such that for\nall i ̸= j satisfying 1 ≤ i, j ≤ n, we have P (zi, zj) = 0 if and only\nif there is an edge in T joining vi to vj.\nNote, for example, that the total degree of the polynomial\n9X 3Y 4 + XY 5 + X 6 − 2\nis 7 because 7 = 3 + 4.",
